# xLaDe Modes

This directory contains the modes for xLaDe CLI
In easy language, modes are the toggles for enabling and disabling different features in xLaDe.
Features include experiments, policies, scripts, etc.

---

## Modes

We offer 3 modes at this stage 

1. Experimental
2. Stable
3. Onboarding

---

## Experimental

This mode is intended for creating and running experiments.
This mode lets users to run experiments, run scripts, etc.

Due to running of the external scripts and experiments, it may be unstable in nature.
So, we call it experimental.

---

## Stable

This mode disables the running of experiments.
This mode lets users to explore and read the experiments and project safely.

Due to safety and stability, it is stable.
So, we call it stable.

---

## Onboarding

This mode is just for onboarding new users.
We don't encourage users to use it.
This mode can run a few selected experiments to show the use of xLaDe, while blocking others.
This mode is handcrafted for few experiments only.

---

## Current Status

At current, modes are implemented in xLaDe CLI.
But the onboarding mode is not yet implemented.

However, they are in the xLaDe/ directory.
We want to transfer them here for modularity, and keep the modes separate from core CLI.
If you are a contributor with some experience, then only help in this, as it may break CLI.

--- 
